# atomic sandbox scene v1
# n-Butane (anti, C2h), relaxed on this solver's default surface: FIRE (the app's Relax) at the Accurate grid
# (h = sigma = 0.15 Bohr) under the accepted pseudopotentials, GPU teacher at tol 1e-6, stopped at max|F| 2e-3 Ha/Bohr or
# 60 steps, whichever first (M8a ruling P22: a near-equilibrium geometry for the capping gate) - stopped at max|F| <= 2e-3.
# Start geometry only (relaxed by this solver): all staggered, C-C 1.53 A, CCC 113 degrees (about the gas-phase
# electron-diffraction structure, Bradford, Fitzwater & Bartell, J. Mol. Struct. 38, 185 (1977)), C-H 1.09 A, tetrahedral
# methyl H, HCH 107 degrees on CH2; the geometry below is this solver's, not experiment.
# Relaxed: 27 FIRE steps, E = -29.237850 Ha, max|F| = 1.4e-3 Ha/Bohr re-centred; C-C 2.8544, 2.8605, 2.8544 Bohr.
# Box: the nuclei's extent + 4 Bohr per side at h = 0.15 (125^3). Written by validate/tests/capping.rs relax_butane.
grid 125 0.15
charge 0
ionic accepted
